        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: The Jargon Society\n- People: Louis Zukofsky, Charles Olson, Paul Metcalf, James Broughton, Jonathan Williams\n- Projects: Objectivist group of poets\n- Products: White Trash Cooking\n- Topics: American literary avant-garde, folk art\n\nFacts:\n- Louis Zukofsky was one of the founders and the primary theorist of the Objectivist group of poets.\n- Louis Zukofsky became an important influence on subsequent generations of poets in America and abroad.\n- The Jargon Society published seminal works of the American literary avant-garde.\n- The Jargon Society published books by Charles Olson, Louis Zukofsky, Paul Metcalf, James Broughton, and Jonathan Williams.\n- The Jargon Society also published sui generis folk art books such as White Trash Cooking.",
